{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.668,
            0.064,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Perimeter and Area"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.122,
            0.249,
            0.147
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "6.2 Area"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.162,
            0.833,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "We have studied the areas of closed figures (regular and irregular) in previous grades. Let us recall some key points."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.208,
            0.831,
            0.23
          ],
          "content": "The amount of region enclosed by a closed figure is called its **area**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.232,
            0.834,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": "In previous grades, we arrived at the formula for the area of a rectangle and a square using square grid paper. Do you remember?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.3,
            0.329,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "Area of a square ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.499,
            0.3,
            0.708,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": "Area of a rectangle ="
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.402,
            0.348,
            0.575,
            0.368
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Teacher’s Note"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.373,
            0.789,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "Help students in recalling the method of finding the area of a rectangle and a square using grid papers. Provide square grid papers to students and let them come up with the formula."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.456,
            0.729,
            0.478
          ],
          "content": "Let’s see some real-life problems related to these ideas."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.488,
            0.833,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": "**Example:** A floor is 5 m long and 4 m wide. A square carpet of sides 3 m is laid on the floor. Find the area of the floor that is not carpeted."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.538,
            0.209,
            0.558
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.562,
            0.37,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "Length of the floor = 5 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.587,
            0.367,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": "Width of the floor = 4 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.613,
            0.665,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "Area of the floor = length × width = 5 m × 4 m = 20 sq m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.638,
            0.458,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "Length of the square carpet = 3 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.663,
            0.673,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": "Area of the carpet = length × length = 3 m × 3 m = 9 sq m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.689,
            0.645,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "Hence, the area of the floor laid with carpet is 9 sq m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.714,
            0.833,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the area of the floor that is not carpeted is: area of the floor minus the area of the floor laid with carpet = 20 sq m – 9 sq m = 11 sq m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.768,
            0.835,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": "**Example:** Four square flower beds each of side 4 m are in four corners on a piece of land 12 m long and 10 m wide. Find the area of the remaining part of the land."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.885,
            0.941,
            0.917,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": ""
        },
        {
